From: LuneOS
Subject: [PATCH] PalmSystem: fix banner removal

removeBannerMessage() and clearBannerMessages() call
luna://org.webosports.notifications/close and /closeAll. No such service
exists on the bus - the only notification service is com.webos.notification,
which is what AddBannerMessage() itself calls to create the toast. Both calls
are therefore dropped and a banner an application withdraws stays put.
Checked against the running service:

    createToast {"message":"..."}   -> {"returnValue":true,
                                        "toastId":"<appId>-<pid>-<ms>"}
    closeToast  {"toastId":"<id>"}  -> {"returnValue":true}
    closeToast  {"id":"<id>"}       -> {"returnValue":false,
                                        "errorText":"Both Toast Id and Source
                                         Id can't be Empty"}

so the parameter is "toastId", not "id". closeToast also takes a "sourceId",
which is the bulk form clearBannerMessages() wants. createToast ignores a
caller-supplied toastId, so the id has to come back from the reply.

Two things stopped that reply from ever arriving. LSCalloutContext cancels its
call from its destructor, and the context was a local:

    LSCalloutContext cbAddBanner(lambda);
    ...Call(..., &cbAddBanner);          // cancelled on return

so the toastId was never recorded and there was nothing to close. It is now
held in a map for the lifetime of the call, the same way
notification_service_luna.cc owns the contexts for its own createToast calls.

The id bookkeeping was wrong too. currentNotifId is a static local, and the
callback read it rather than the value belonging to its own call:

    bannerIds_[currentNotifId++] = "no-uuid";      // writes slot N
    ... [this](payload) {
      this->bannerIds_[currentNotifId] = ...       // writes slot N+1
    }

The placeholder landed in a slot nothing reads, and a second banner posted
before the first reply would corrupt the mapping. The id is now captured by
value, and the slot is left empty until the reply lands so that removing a
banner whose createToast has not answered yet is a no-op rather than a close
call with an empty toastId.

closeToast sits in the notification.management group while createToast is in
notification.operation, so com.palm.webappmanager needs the former added to
its client permissions or the call is refused with

    LS_REQUIRES_SECURITY {"CLIENT":"com.palm.webappmanager",
                          "SERVICE":"com.webos.notification",
                          "METHOD":"closeToast"}

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific; fixes a LuneOS patch]

--- a/src/platform/webengine/palm_system_blink.cc
+++ b/src/platform/webengine/palm_system_blink.cc
@@ -27,6 +27,13 @@
 
 namespace {
 
+// LSCalloutContext cancels its call from its destructor, so a context created
+// on the stack cancels the moment the calling function returns and its reply
+// is never delivered. Keep banner contexts alive here, keyed by banner id -
+// the same ownership pattern notification_service_luna.cc uses for its own
+// createToast calls.
+std::map<int, LSCalloutContext> banner_contexts;
+
 const char* toStr(const bool value) {
   return value ? "true" : "false";
 }
@@ -267,31 +274,50 @@
 
   static int currentNotifId = 0; // always increment a static int, to return a unique id
 
-  bannerIds_[currentNotifId++] = "no-uuid";
-  std::function<Json::Value(const Json::Value&)> lambda = [this](const Json::Value& payload) {
-      this->bannerIds_[currentNotifId] = payload["toastId"].asString();
-      return payload;
-  };
-  LSCalloutContext cbAddBanner(lambda);
+  const int bannerId = ++currentNotifId; // ids start at 1, so 0 can mean "none"
+
+  // Left empty until createToast answers. RemoveBannerMessage() treats an
+  // empty entry as "not created yet" rather than closing toastId "".
+  bannerIds_[bannerId] = std::string();
+
+  // bannerId is captured by value: currentNotifId is a static local and will
+  // have moved on by the time this reply arrives if another banner was posted
+  // in the meantime.
+  banner_contexts.emplace(
+      bannerId, LSCalloutContext([this, bannerId](const Json::Value& payload) {
+        if (payload.isObject() && payload["toastId"].isString()) {
+          this->bannerIds_[bannerId] = payload["toastId"].asString();
+        }
+        banner_contexts.erase(bannerId);
+        return Json::Value();
+      }));
 
   WebAppManagerServiceLuna::Instance()->Call(
-      "luna://com.webos.notification/createToast", create_params, app_->AppId().c_str(), &cbAddBanner);
+      "luna://com.webos.notification/createToast", create_params,
+      app_->AppId().c_str(), &banner_contexts.at(bannerId));
 
-  return currentNotifId;
+  return bannerId;
 }
 
 void PalmSystemBlink::RemoveBannerMessage(std::string id) {
-  std::string remove_params = R"(
-    {"id" : ")" + bannerIds_[std::atoi(id.c_str())] + R"("}
-  )";
+  const auto it = bannerIds_.find(std::atoi(id.c_str()));
+  if (it == bannerIds_.end() || it->second.empty()) {
+    // Unknown banner, or createToast has not returned its id yet.
+    return;
+  }
 
-  app_->ServiceCall("luna://org.webosports.notifications/close", remove_params, app_->AppId());
+  std::string remove_params = R"({"toastId":")" + it->second + R"("})";
+
+  app_->ServiceCall("luna://com.webos.notification/closeToast", remove_params, app_->AppId());
+  bannerIds_.erase(it);
 }
-void PalmSystemBlink::ClearBannerMessages() {
 
-  std::string clear_params = "{}";
+void PalmSystemBlink::ClearBannerMessages() {
+  // closeToast's bulk form: drop everything this application posted.
+  std::string clear_params = R"({"sourceId":")" + app_->AppId() + R"("})";
 
-  app_->ServiceCall("luna://org.webosports.notifications/closeAll", clear_params, app_->AppId());
+  app_->ServiceCall("luna://com.webos.notification/closeToast", clear_params, app_->AppId());
+  bannerIds_.clear();
 }
 
 Json::Value PalmSystemBlink::Initialize() {
